.TH INSTALL 8 2026-11-03 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
install \- install or update DarqOS from an unpacked distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /darq/dist/darq/bin/install
.RB [ \-\-boot ]
.br
.B /darq/bin/install
.RB [ \-\-boot ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B install
installs DarqOS from the unpacked distribution it's in, normally
.IR /darq/dist/darq ,
into the installation root,
.IR /darq ,
and prepares the host to run it.
It is normally run by
.BR dui (8),
as root, on Debian 13 (trixie).
The same command installs and updates.
.PP
Run from the installation itself, as
.BR "/darq/bin/install \-\-boot" ,
it does every step but copying the code (step 4), which is already
there.
.PP
It performs these steps, stopping if any fails:
.IP 1. 4
Stop DarqOS
.RI ( darqos-pkernel.service ),
if it's running.
.IP 2.
Install the Debian packages DarqOS needs: to build the compositor
(wlroots 0.18 and its build tools), the libraries Qt needs, Python
3.13's
.BR venv ,
polkit (without which logind lets only root power the machine off or
reboot it),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
and
.BR rsync (1).
.IP 3.
Create the
.B darq
user, if it doesn't exist.
.IP 4.
Copy the code into
.IR /darq ,
as source, owned by root and writable only by root, whatever its
modes in the distribution, with
.BR "rsync \-\-delete" ,
so what's gone from the distribution goes, with its compiled
.I __pycache__
too, while the caches of what's still there are kept; its
.IR VERSION ,
and its release notes, as
.IR /darq/RELEASE_NOTES.md ;
and the manual pages, by section.
.IP 5.
Build the compositor, in
.IR /darq/compositor/build .
.IP 6.
Make or update the Python environment,
.IR /darq/env ,
from the distribution's
.IR requirements.txt ,
and compile the code.
An environment using the system's site packages, as earlier installs
made, is made again.
.IP 7.
Create the run directory,
.IR /darq/run ,
owned by
.BR darq ,
mode 0700.
.IP 8.
Copy the
.BR systemd (1)
units into
.IR /etc/systemd/system ,
and create
.I /etc/darqos/backup.conf
if it doesn't exist.
.IP 9.
Enable the daily backup,
.IR darqos-backup.timer .
.IP 10.
With
.BR \-\-boot ,
enable the p-kernel's unit, and make
.I darqos.target
the default boot target.
.IP 11.
Start DarqOS again, if it was running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-boot
Make DarqOS the machine's default boot.
Without it, DarqOS starts only when asked
.RB ( "systemctl start darqos-pkernel" ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARQ
Installation root.
Default:
.IR /darq .
.TP
.B LOG_DIR
Where the install is logged.
Default:
.IR /var/log/darqos .
.TP
.B DARQOS_INSTALL_SKIP
For tests: the steps to skip, separated by spaces: any of
.BR root " (the check for it),"
.BR stop ,
.BR packages ,
.BR user ,
.BR owner " (of the run directory),"
.BR compositor ,
.BR venv ,
.BR units ,
.BR backup ,
.B boot
and
.BR start .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /darq/dist/darq
The unpacked distribution.
.TP
.I /darq/VERSION
The installed distribution's version, commit and date.
.TP
.I /darq/env
Python virtual environment.
.TP
.I /darq/run
The run directory: databases, and the boot vector.
It isn't changed by an update.
.TP
.I /darq/kernel
The p-kernel
.RI ( pkernel ),
Python loader
.RI ( pyloader ),
launcher script
.RI ( darqos-pkernel ),
and the
.B systemd
units:
.IR darqos-pkernel.service ,
.IR darqos.target ,
.I darqos-backup.service
and
.IR darqos-backup.timer .
.TP
.I /etc/darqos/backup.conf
Backup configuration: see
.BR darqos-backup (8).
.TP
.I /darq/man
Installed manual pages; read them with
.BR "man \-M /darq/man" .
.TP
.I /var/log/darqos/install-*.log
Each install's output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if it installed; 1 if a step failed; 2 for a bad option.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is written to standard output, and the log, as lines starting
.RB \(lq Ok: \(rq,
and errors as lines starting
.RB \(lq Error: \(rq.
.SH BUGS
Storage in the run directory isn't yet migrated to a new version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR darqos-backup (8),
.BR dui (8),
.BR pkernel (8)
